  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through Saturday)\nIssued at 317 AM EDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nThe front lingers across far southern Georgia into northern\nFlorida Tuesday and Wednesday with high pressure in its wake \nbringing drier and cooler conditions to the area through midweek. \nTemperatures will drop to more seasonal levels briefly, though \nquickly rebounding by late week. Still, several days with lows in \nthe 50s (and 40s in the mountains) and highs back in the 70s to \nlow-to-mid 80s amid much lower humidity will bring a decidedly \nmore fall-like feel to things.\n\nModels continue to trend back to a wetter and more active weather\npattern by the tail end of the forecast period next weekend as the\nfrontal boundary surges back northward bringing Gulf moisture back\ninto the area. Details remain uncertain at this juncture, but \na return to a rainy/more active pattern could unfortunately \ncoincide with another weekend.",
